---
code: lint-tool-absent
when-fires: a configured external linter is not on PATH, so its checks did not run. lint/source_external.rs. `{tool}` is the tool name.
why: 27R §4 dir-absent-is-info - a missing tool is the admin's environment, disclosed rather than silently skipped; --require-tools raises it to a hard CI error. The replay is the real `dorc lint` surface with tools left ENABLED; the injected runner (the one external-tool DI seam) answers every tool absent, so an airgapped machine's own output is reached with no PATH probe and no process.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# Nothing here for any NATIVE lint source to report: what the case is about is the two external
# tools, which this run leaves enabled and the injected runner answers absent.
nginx__is_converged() {
   systemctl is-active --quiet nginx
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh
dorc lint findings (advisory; the machine format `--format=jsonl` is the stable surface):

(run):
  - info [checkbashisms:lint-tool-absent] Dorc did not find `checkbashisms` on PATH, so none of its checks ran. Install it, pass --no-tools to silence this note, or --require-tools to make a missing tool a hard error. (raw)
  - info [shellcheck:lint-tool-absent] Dorc did not find `shellcheck` on PATH, so none of its checks ran. Install it, pass --no-tools to silence this note, or --require-tools to make a missing tool a hard error. (raw)

dorc lint: 0 errors, 0 warnings, 2 infos across 1 file.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: lint-tool-absent
{{tool}} = "checkbashisms"
{{v0}} = "0"
{{v1}} = "s"
{{v2}} = "0"
{{v3}} = "s"
{{v4}} = "2"
{{v5}} = "s"
{{v6}} = "1"
{{v7}} = ""
